chronyc display resolution: picoseconds and ppt, auto-scaled units (chrony 4.9)

Companion to chrony49-tracking-ppt.patch. chronyc rounds the daemon's numbers away:
tracking shows offsets at 9 decimals (ns) and frequencies at 3 (ppb); sources/sourcestats
print whole nanoseconds. The command protocol's Float carries a 25-bit coefficient
(~7 significant digits), so the hidden digits are real: a 3.6e-9 s offset is exact to
~2e-16 s, residual freq and skew to ~1e-10 ppm.

- tracking: times and frequencies print with an auto-scaled unit instead of a fixed
  column of zeroes -- whole picoseconds below 1 ns, then three decimals of ns/us/ms/s;
  whole ppt below 1 ppb, then three decimals of ppb/ppm:
      System time     : 118 ps slow of NTP time
      Last offset     : -460 ps
      RMS offset      : 1.342 ns
      Frequency       : 56.465 ppb slow
      Residual freq   : -2 ppt
      Skew            : 312 ppt
      Root dispersion : 6.057 us
- sources / sourcestats / selectdata (fixed-width tables): values under 10 ns print in
  picoseconds ("-1463ps[-1895ps]", "Std Dev 5236ps") in the same column width; the
  frequency columns carry a unit in the same 10 characters ("   -2ppt", "+56.47ppb",
  " +7.475ppm").
- CSV mode (-c) stays numeric: seconds at 12 decimals, ppm at 6.
Parsers that assume an "ns" suffix must accept "ps" (deploy/pi5/pps-soaklog.sh does).

